<spell-notebook "breadcrumb usage">
	<header level="1">
		Breadcrumb
		<header>A breadcrumb is used to show hierarchy between content.</>
	</>
	<breadcrumb-tab-bar showing="usage"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#using-it">Using it</>
				<ui-item link="#events">Events</>
				<ui-item link="#keyboard">Keyboard</>
				<ui-item link="#accessibility">Accessibility</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- USAGE:  how to use it (sections, dividers), keyboard, accessibility. -->
	<section label="Using it">
		<markdown>
			`<ui-breadcrumbs>` is a `<nav>` around an ordered list; each `<ui-breadcrumb>` is one item of it.

			- A section with `link` is a link (`target` works too); one without is plain text.
			- An `active` section is the current page: bold, never a link, even with `link`.
			- Each section draws its own divider before it (hidden on the first), so there is nothing to put between them.
			- `divider` sets the text divider (`/` when unset); `divider-icon` draws an icon instead, in the text colour.
			- `size` and `inverted` are the only look words.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```html
			<ui-breadcrumbs aria-label="Location" divider-icon="chevron right">
			  <ui-breadcrumb link="/">Home</ui-breadcrumb>
			  <ui-breadcrumb link="/store">Store</ui-breadcrumb>
			  <ui-breadcrumb selected>T-Shirt</ui-breadcrumb>
			</ui-breadcrumbs>
			```
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Events">
		<markdown>
			Breadcrumbs have no events of their own: a linked section is a real `<a>`, so it fires the native `click` and
			navigates.
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Keyboard">
		<markdown>
			- **Tab** / **Shift+Tab** moves between the linked sections; text and `active` sections are not tab stops.
			- **Enter** follows the focused link.
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Accessibility">
		<markdown>
			- The WAI-ARIA breadcrumb pattern: a `<nav>` landmark around an `<ol>`, whose items are the sections.
			- The landmark is named "Breadcrumb" (translatable); an `aria-label` on the host replaces it. Give each breadcrumb
			  on a page its own name.
			- The `active` section carries `aria-current="page"`. Linked sections are real `<a>`s: focusable, with Enter to
			  follow.
			- Dividers are drawn by CSS and hidden from assistive technology, so the list reads as its section names only.
			- If the element fails to render, it shows its sections through a bare `<slot>`, so their text and
			  links stay; the dividers between them, the `<nav>` around them and its "Breadcrumb" name go.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
